{"id":"mahabharata-3-051","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":51,"title":"एकपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 51 · The gods ask Nala to be their messenger","summary":{"en":"Damayanti pines for Nala, and her father Bhima announces her svayamvara. Narada tells Indra, and Indra, Agni, Varuna and Yama set out to woo her; meeting Nala on the way, they ask him to be their messenger.","kn":"ದಮಯಂತಿ ನಳನಿಗಾಗಿ ಹಂಬಲಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ, ತಂದೆ ಭೀಮರಾಜನು ಅವಳ ಸ್ವಯಂವರ ಘೋಷಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ನಾರದರು ಇಂದ್ರನಿಗೆ ತಿಳಿಸಿದಾಗ ಇಂದ್ರ, ಅಗ್ನಿ, ವರುಣ, ಯಮರು ಅವಳನ್ನು ವರಿಸಲು ಹೊರಡುತ್ತಾರೆ; ದಾರಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ನಳನನ್ನು ಕಂಡು ತಮ್ಮ ದೂತನಾಗೆಂದು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"दमयन्ती नल के लिए तरसती हैं, और उनके पिता भीम उनके स्वयंवर की घोषणा करते हैं। नारद इन्द्र को बताते हैं, और इन्द्र, अग्नि, वरुण और यम उन्हें वरने निकलते हैं; मार्ग में नल से मिलकर वे उनसे अपना दूत बनने को कहते हैं।","te":"దమయంతి నలుని కోసం తపిస్తుంది, ఆమె తండ్రి భీమరాజు ఆమె స్వయంవరాన్ని ప్రకటిస్తాడు. నారదుడు ఇంద్రునికి చెప్పగా ఇంద్రుడు, అగ్ని, వరుణుడు, యముడు ఆమెను వరించడానికి బయలుదేరుతారు; దారిలో నలుని కలిసి తమ దూతగా ఉండమని అడుగుతారు.","ta":"தமயந்தி நளனுக்காக ஏங்க, அவள் தந்தை பீம மன்னன் அவள் ஸ்வயம்வரத்தை அறிவிக்கிறான். நாரதர் இந்திரனிடம் சொல்ல, இந்திரன், அக்னி, வருணன், யமன் அவளை மணக்கப் புறப்படுகிறார்கள்; வழியில் நளனைச் சந்தித்துத் தம் தூதனாகுமாறு கேட்கிறார்கள்.","ml":"വിരഹവേദനയോടെ നളനെയോർത്ത് ദമയന്തി കഴിയുന്നു; അവളുടെ പിതാവ് ഭീമൻ സ്വയംവരം പ്രഖ്യാപിക്കുന്നു. നാരദൻ ഇന്ദ്രനോട് വിവരം പറയുന്നു; ഇന്ദ്രൻ, അഗ്നി, വരുണൻ, യമൻ എന്നിവർ അവളെ വിവാഹം ചെയ്യാൻ പുറപ്പെടുന്നു; വഴിയിൽ നളനെ കണ്ട് തങ്ങളുടെ ദൂതനാകാൻ അവർ ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.51; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"इन्द्रलोकाभिगमनपर्व","titleEn":"Indralokabhigamana Parva (Journey to Indra's world)","verses":[{"text":"बृहदश्व उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brihadashva said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"दमयन्ती तु तच्छ्रुत्वा वचो हंसस्य भारत ।\nतदा प्रभृति नस्वस्था नलं प्रति बभूव सा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Descendant of Bharata, from the moment Damayanti heard the swan's words, she was no longer at ease because of Nala."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततश्चिन्तापरा दीना विवर्णवदना कृशा ।\nबभूव दमयन्ती तु निःश्वासपरमा तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Damayanti became distracted and wretched, pale in face and thin, her breath coming in sighs."}},{"n":3,"text":"ऊर्ध्वदृष्टिर्ध्यानपरा बभूवोन्मत्तदर्शना ।\nन शय्यासनभोगेषु रतिं विन्दति कर्हिचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"She gazed upward, absorbed in thought, with a look as of madness, and found no pleasure in bed, seat or enjoyment."}},{"n":4,"text":"न नक्तं न दिवा शेते हा हेति वदती मुहुः ।\nतामस्वस्थां तदाकारां सख्यस्ता जज्ञुरिङ्गितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"She slept neither by night nor by day, and kept crying \"Alas, alas.\" Her friends understood from her signs that she was unwell and in that condition."}},{"n":5,"text":"ततो विदर्भपतये दमयन्त्याः सखीगणः ।\nन्यवेदयत नस्वस्थां दमयन्तीं नरेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the group of Damayanti's friends told the lord of Vidarbha, O king, that Damayanti was unwell."}},{"n":6,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा नृपतिर्भीमो दमयन्तीसखीगणात् ।\nचिन्तयामास तत्कार्यं सुमहत्स्वां सुतां प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this from her friends, King Bhima considered what great matter this was concerning his daughter."}},{"n":7,"text":"स समीक्ष्य महीपालः स्वां सुतां प्राप्तयौवनाम् ।\nअपश्यदात्मनः कार्यं दमयन्त्याः स्वयंवरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king, seeing that his daughter had come of age, saw that what must be done was a svayamvara for Damayanti."}},{"n":8,"text":"स संनिपातयामास महीपालान्विशां पते ।\nअनुभूयतामयं वीराः स्वयंवर इति प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"He gathered the rulers of the earth, lord of people, saying, \"Heroes, come and experience this svayamvara.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"श्रुत्वा तु पार्थिवाः सर्वे दमयन्त्याः स्वयंवरम् ।\nअभिजग्मुस्तदा भीमं राजानो भीमशासनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing of Damayanti's svayamvara, all the kings then came to Bhima, at Bhima's summons."}},{"n":10,"text":"हस्त्यश्वरथघोषेण नादयन्तो वसुंधराम् ।\nविचित्रमाल्याभरणैर्बलैर्दृश्यैः स्वलंकृतैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They made the earth resound with the noise of elephants, horses and chariots, with wonderful garlands and ornaments and splendid armies richly decked."}},{"n":11,"text":"एतस्मिन्नेव काले तु पुराणावृषिसत्तमौ ।\nअटमानौ महात्मानाविन्द्रलोकमितो गतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that very time two ancient best of sages, great souls wandering about, went from here to Indra's world."}},{"n":12,"text":"नारदः पर्वतश्चैव महात्मानौ महाव्रतौ ।\nदेवराजस्य भवनं विविशाते सुपूजितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were the great souls Narada and Parvata, of great vows. Well honored, they entered the palace of the king of the gods."}},{"n":13,"text":"तावर्चित्वा सहस्राक्षस्ततः कुशलमव्ययम् ।\nपप्रच्छानामयं चापि तयोः सर्वगतं विभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The thousand-eyed lord honored them, then asked after their unfailing welfare and the health of everything pertaining to them."}},{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"आवयोः कुशलं देव सर्वत्रगतमीश्वर ।\nलोके च मघवन्कृत्स्ने नृपाः कुशलिनो विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord, all is well with us everywhere, and in the whole world, Maghavan, the kings are well too."}},{"text":"बृहदश्व उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brihadashva said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"नारदस्य वचः श्रुत्वा पप्रच्छ बलवृत्रहा ।\nधर्मज्ञाः पृथिवीपालास्त्यक्तजीवितयोधिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Narada's words, the slayer of Bala and Vritra asked: \"Those earth-rulers who know dharma, who fight giving up their lives,"}},{"n":16,"text":"शस्त्रेण निधनं काले ये गच्छन्त्यपराङ्मुखाः ।\nअयं लोकोऽक्षयस्तेषां यथैव मम कामधुक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"who meet death by the sword in time without turning away, for them is an imperishable world, like a wish-granting cow for me."}},{"n":17,"text":"क्व नु ते क्षत्रियाः शूरा न हि पश्यामि तानहम् ।\nआगच्छतो महीपालानतिथीन्दयितान्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where are those brave kshatriyas? I do not see them, my beloved guests, the rulers of earth coming here.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु शक्रेण नारदः प्रत्यभाषत ।\nशृणु मे भगवन्येन न दृश्यन्ते महीक्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Spoken to thus by Shakra, Narada replied: \"Listen, blessed one, to why the kings are not seen."}},{"n":19,"text":"विदर्भराजदुहिता दमयन्तीति विश्रुता ।\nरूपेण समतिक्रान्ता पृथिव्यां सर्वयोषितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is the daughter of the king of Vidarbha, famed as Damayanti, who surpasses all women on earth in beauty."}},{"n":20,"text":"तस्याः स्वयंवरः शक्र भविता नचिरादिव ।\nतत्र गच्छन्ति राजानो राजपुत्राश्च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Her svayamvara will be held, Shakra, very soon, and kings and princes are going there from everywhere."}},{"n":21,"text":"तां रत्नभूतां लोकस्य प्रार्थयन्तो महीक्षितः ।\nकाङ्क्षन्ति स्म विशेषेण बलवृत्रनिषूदन ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth's rulers, seeking her as the world's jewel, especially long for her, slayer of Bala and Vritra.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"एतस्मिन्कथ्यमाने तु लोकपालाश्च साग्निकाः ।\nआजग्मुर्देवराजस्य समीपममरोत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While this was being told, the world-guardians with Agni, the best of immortals, came near the king of the gods."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततस्तच्छुश्रुवुः सर्वे नारदस्य वचो महत् ।\nश्रुत्वा चैवाब्रुवन्हृष्टा गच्छामो वयमप्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all of them heard Narada's great words, and having heard, they said gladly, \"We too will go.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"ततः सर्वे महाराज सगणाः सहवाहनाः ।\nविदर्भानभितो जग्मुर्यत्र सर्वे महीक्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all of them, great king, with their attendants and mounts, went to Vidarbha where all the kings were."}},{"n":25,"text":"नलोऽपि राजा कौन्तेय श्रुत्वा राज्ञां समागमम् ।\nअभ्यगच्छददीनात्मा दमयन्तीमनुव्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Nala too, Kaunteya, hearing of the gathering of kings, set out in good spirits, devoted to Damayanti."}},{"n":26,"text":"अथ देवाः पथि नलं ददृशुर्भूतले स्थितम् ।\nसाक्षादिव स्थितं मूर्त्या मन्मथं रूपसंपदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then on the road the gods saw Nala standing on the ground, as if Manmatha himself were standing there in body, with wealth of beauty."}},{"n":27,"text":"तं दृष्ट्वा लोकपालास्ते भ्राजमानं यथा रविम् ।\nतस्थुर्विगतसंकल्पा विस्मिता रूपसंपदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him shining like the sun, the world-guardians stopped, their purpose forgotten, amazed at his beauty."}},{"n":28,"text":"ततोऽन्तरिक्षे विष्टभ्य विमानानि दिवौकसः ।\nअब्रुवन्नैषधं राजन्नवतीर्य नभस्तलात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the sky-dwellers halted their celestial cars in the air, came down from the heavens, and spoke to the Nishadha king."}},{"n":29,"text":"भो भो नैषध राजेन्द्र नल सत्यव्रतो भवान् ।\nअस्माकं कुरु साहाय्यं दूतो भव नरोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Nala, Nishadha, best of kings, you are firm in truth. Help us; be our messenger, best of men.\""}}]}]}